check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5066287Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5074553Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5160392Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5168655Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5169334Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5170216Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5170489Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5170812Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5171406Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5171765Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5172000Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5172974Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5173332Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5173789Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5174531Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5175322Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5175763Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5176002Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5176598Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5176953Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5177213Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5177700Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5177956Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5178100Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5178326Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5178956Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5179715Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5180044Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5180196Z I will:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5180435Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5180713Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5181301Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5181812Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5182447Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5182834Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5183170Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5183702Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5184128Z    /root
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5193845Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5194552Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5203190Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5203964Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5204289Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5205160Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5205861Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5221348Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5222193Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5230447Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5231313Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5231827Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5232065Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5232350Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5232696Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5232968Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5233502Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5233800Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5234004Z If you would like to
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5234386Z see the output, try like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5234597Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5234875Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5235365Z   $ sh ./install-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5235626Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.5235640Z 
