project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5546816Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5555660Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5643896Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5652664Z ^[[0m
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5653147Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5653738Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5654032Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5654283Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5654877Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5655309Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5655990Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5656495Z    if you are ready to continue.
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5656743Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5657147Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5657845Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5658294Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5658595Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5658744Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5659030Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5659239Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5659407Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5659720Z    can use Nix.
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5659843Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5659932Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5660078Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5660311Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5660684Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5663306Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5663468Z I will:
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5663719Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5665454Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5666333Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5666742Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5667086Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5667469Z  - install Nix in /nix
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5667850Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5668380Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5668892Z    /root
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5677046Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5677511Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5687824Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5688271Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5688574Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5689772Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5690507Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5706481Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5706933Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5715993Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5716643Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5717078Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5717248Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5717390Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5717747Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5717952Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5718290Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5718500Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5718605Z If you would like to
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5718894Z see the output, try like this:
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5719074Z 
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5719273Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
project-sdk-closure	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.5719676Z   $ sh ./install-nix
