composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0272430Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0284203Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0391908Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0416701Z ^[[0m
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0417340Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0418105Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0418445Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0418748Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0419501Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0419965Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0420580Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0421208Z    if you are ready to continue.
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0421518Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0422173Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0422715Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0423143Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0423639Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0423789Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0423948Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0424209Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0424400Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0424774Z    can use Nix.
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0424907Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0424994Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0425146Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0425437Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0425892Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0426078Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0426159Z I will:
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0426267Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0426432Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0426813Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0427201Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0427567Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0427817Z  - install Nix in /nix
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0428064Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0428446Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0428796Z    /root
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0431303Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0432073Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0444026Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0444606Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0444993Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0446721Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0447325Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0466781Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0467465Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0478349Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0479231Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0479885Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0480439Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0480676Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0481056Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0481360Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0482030Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0482384Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0482541Z If you would like to
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0482936Z see the output, try like this:
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0483219Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0483503Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0484059Z   $ sh ./install-nix
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.0484291Z 
