repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3629138Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3638590Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3728879Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3737859Z ^[[0m
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3738878Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3739863Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3740360Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3740848Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3741816Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3742255Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3742870Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3743300Z    if you are ready to continue.
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3743502Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3743933Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3744461Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3744958Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3745330Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3745520Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3745714Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3746018Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3746233Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3746646Z    can use Nix.
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3746792Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3746919Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3747084Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3748163Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3749165Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3752237Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3752489Z I will:
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3752814Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3753157Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3753710Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3754153Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3754563Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3754858Z  - install Nix in /nix
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3755164Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3755897Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3756543Z    /root
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3765311Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3766122Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3775774Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3776725Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3777319Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3777744Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3778437Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3794962Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3795723Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3804312Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3805241Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3805739Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3805978Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3806542Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3806898Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3807370Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3807876Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3808177Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3808388Z If you would like to
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3808671Z see the output, try like this:
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3808894Z 
repository-replay	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3809101Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
