conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8606351Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8615772Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8713806Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8724036Z ^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8724907Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8725552Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8725898Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8726163Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8726725Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8727036Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8727339Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8728433Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8728782Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8729353Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8730089Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8730846Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8731325Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8731617Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8731872Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8732164Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8732400Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8732894Z    can use Nix.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8733077Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8733249Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8733452Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8733961Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8734707Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8738428Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8738677Z I will:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8739260Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8740570Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8741088Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8741706Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8742724Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8743136Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8743567Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8744022Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8744429Z    /root
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8753464Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8754085Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8764324Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8765431Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8765760Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8766138Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8766784Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8785039Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8786442Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8795961Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8796717Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8797189Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8797522Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8797739Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8798042Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8798314Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8798884Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8799117Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8799261Z If you would like to
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8799591Z see the output, try like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8799864Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8800145Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.8800653Z   $ sh ./install-nix
