legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3416177Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3426739Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3538002Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3549406Z ^[[0m
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3550394Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3551394Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3551926Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3552393Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3553920Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3554597Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3555474Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3556334Z    if you are ready to continue.
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3556732Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3557418Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3558487Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3559342Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3560021Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3560340Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3560729Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3561216Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3561593Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3562106Z    can use Nix.
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3562264Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3562396Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3562587Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3563046Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3564396Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3564834Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3565074Z I will:
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3565294Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3565515Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3565981Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3566464Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3566889Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3567201Z  - install Nix in /nix
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3567520Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3567963Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3568393Z    /root
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3580478Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3581297Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3592646Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3593340Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3594090Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3595140Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3595842Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3615262Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3615861Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3626852Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3627501Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3628304Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3628703Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3629360Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3629846Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3630216Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3631267Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3631832Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3632132Z If you would like to
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3632581Z see the output, try like this:
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3632783Z 
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3633018Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
legacy-basic-56	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.3633404Z   $ sh ./install-nix
