conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4421426Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4525536Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4536227Z ^[[0m
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4536622Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4537091Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4537316Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4537506Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4537984Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4538446Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4538646Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4539123Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4539308Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4539930Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4540508Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4541334Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4541891Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4542093Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4542258Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4542531Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4542726Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4543128Z    can use Nix.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4543267Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4543368Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4543523Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4543833Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4544306Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4548994Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4549157Z I will:
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4549349Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4549607Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4550236Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4551329Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4552019Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4552464Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4552880Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4553785Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4554446Z    /root
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4565256Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4566212Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4578585Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:56.4579389Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
