javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1107725Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1119344Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1225643Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1236306Z ^[[0m
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1237069Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1237901Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1238385Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1238756Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1239762Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1240352Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1241159Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1242048Z    if you are ready to continue.
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1242461Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1243388Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1244637Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1245676Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1246196Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1246439Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1246680Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1247051Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1247317Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1247812Z    can use Nix.
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1247985Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1248138Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1248338Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1248727Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1249306Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1249843Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1250042Z I will:
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1250371Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1250732Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1251411Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1251948Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1252472Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1253063Z  - install Nix in /nix
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1253431Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1253935Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1254344Z    /root
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1266105Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1267091Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1278476Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1279052Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1279561Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1280905Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1281602Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1301237Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1301819Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1312811Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1313602Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1314437Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1314845Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1315393Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1315865Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1316253Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1317192Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1317846Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1318144Z If you would like to
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1318522Z see the output, try like this:
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1318745Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1318953Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1319418Z   $ sh ./install-nix
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1319615Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1319624Z 
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1319910Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1327240Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1327762Z been installed on this system.
javadoc-link-metadata	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:53.1374961Z 
