conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6742571Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6743430Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6750552Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6750724Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6751420Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6751924Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6752612Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6752945Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6753137Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6753310Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6753536Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6753712Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6754096Z    can use Nix.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6754250Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6754390Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6754517Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6754786Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6755232Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6755413Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6755559Z I will:
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6755800Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6755981Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6756341Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6756722Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6757087Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6757397Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6757703Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6758059Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6758389Z    /root
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6769761Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6770426Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6778213Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:51.6778856Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
