conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2810922Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2821908Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2934445Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2945317Z ^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2946054Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2946977Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2947434Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2947857Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2948849Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2949434Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2949845Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2950632Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2951027Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2952256Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2953653Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2954593Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2955565Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2955921Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2956285Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2956820Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2957229Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2957875Z    can use Nix.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2958229Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2958381Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2958625Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2959005Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2959612Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2960499Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2960724Z I will:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2961273Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2961690Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2962512Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2963651Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2964445Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2965062Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2965465Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2966013Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2966534Z    /root
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2977895Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2978735Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2990881Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2991762Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2992084Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2992871Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.2993806Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3013635Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3014471Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3025219Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3026186Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3026713Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3026948Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3027166Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3027666Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3028041Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3028522Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
