conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3489418Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3497239Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3587515Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3596303Z ^[[0m
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3597399Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3598168Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3598608Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3598933Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3599656Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3600198Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3600545Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3601306Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3601718Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3603051Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3603875Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3604473Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3605090Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3605336Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3605550Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3605877Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3606118Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3606623Z    can use Nix.
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3606799Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3607000Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3607233Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3607655Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3608192Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3609142Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3609344Z I will:
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3610011Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3613101Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3613849Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3615190Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3615741Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3616459Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3617112Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3617662Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3618214Z    /root
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3624901Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3625767Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3635304Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3636165Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3636647Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3637160Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3637873Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3654119Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3655199Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3663233Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3664158Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3664979Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T20:46:52.3665390Z 
